    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nForkin Earls Property are delighted to present A truly exceptional coastal residence with Private beach access.\n\nWavecrest is set behind elegant wrought-iron gates within beautifully landscaped private gardens, this outstanding four-bedroom, three bathroom detached home offers an exceptional blend of contemporary comfort, timeless design and one of the finest coastal settings on Ireland's east coast.\n\nLocated in the heart of Brittas Bay, the property enjoys private gated access directly onto the sand dunes and renowned Blue Flag beach, creating a lifestyle where morning walks, family beach days and peaceful seaside living become part of everyday life.\n\nExtending to approximately 181 sq.m. (1,948 sq.ft.), the home has been finished to an exceptional standard throughout. At its heart is a stunning open-plan kitchen, dining and living space with vaulted ceilings and a feature multi-fuel stove. The bespoke kitchen boasts marble worktops, premium integrated appliances and flows seamlessly into a light-filled sunroom overlooking the gardens and sunny patio.\nThere are four generous double bedrooms, including a superb principal suite with vaulted ceiling, exposed timber beams, fitted wardrobes, patio access and an elegant en-suite. A stylish family bathroom, guest shower room and fully fitted utility room complete the accommodation.\n\nThe beautifully landscaped gardens provide outstanding privacy, with mature trees, colourful planting and generous outdoor entertaining space. A luxurious spa pool, timber log cabin, detached storage sheds and private beach access combine to create a truly exceptional outdoor setting.\n\nThe home also offers impressive energy efficiency, featuring triple-glazed windows and doors, a dual heating system with condensing oil-fired boiler and multi-fuel stove with back boiler, a 6kW solar PV system with 5kW battery storage, and a Zappi electric vehicle charging point.\n\nPerfectly positioned just three minutes from the M11 (Exit 19, Jack White's), the property is within walking distance of the village shop, café, McDaniel's pub, church, primary school and beach, while Wicklow Town is approximately 15 minutes away and Dublin is easily accessible. The area is surrounded by top 100 golf courses including the world famous European Club (ranked #2 in Ireland in 2024) is just over 2km from the property.\n\nThe generous site also offers excellent potential to extend, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nA rare opportunity to acquire an exceptional coastal home where privacy, quality and direct beach access combine to create one of Brittas Bay's most desirable residential offerings.\n\nViewings are highly recommended and are strictly by appointment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nAccommodation: - \n\n\nOpen-Plan Kitchen / Living / Dining Room: - 9.45m x 8.94m\nA magnificent vaulted living space with exposed timber beams, feature fireplace with multi-fuel stove, bespoke fitted kitchen with marble worktops and premium integrated appliances. Sliding doors open to the sunroom and patio for effortless indoor-outdoor living.\n\nEntrance Hall: - \nA bright and welcoming entrance hall with timber flooring and a large picture window overlooking the front gardens.\n\nSunroom: - 6.41m x 3.06m\nA light-filled space overlooking the landscaped rear gardens with direct access to the patio.\n\nUtility Room: - 2.6m x 2.41m\nFully fitted with additional storage, sink, plumbing for a washing machine and space for an additional fridge freezer.\n\nPrincipal Bedroom: - 5.6m x 5.11m\nA spacious vaulted bedroom with fitted wardrobes, garden access and a beautifully appointed en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite: - 3.2m x 2.36m\nFreestanding bath, WC, wash hand basin and elegant marble finishes.\n\nBedroom Two: - 4.56m x 3.2m\nAnother spacious double bedroom enjoying dual-aspect windows that fill the room with natural light. Built-in wardrobes provide excellent storage, while carpet flooring adds warmth and comfort.\n\nBedroom Three: - 3.63m x 3.2m\nA bright double bedroom overlooking the front garden, finished with carpet flooring and offering excellent versatility as a guest bedroom, children's room or home office.\n\nBedrooms Four: - 3.02m x 2.94m\nA generously proportioned double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, complete with carpet flooring and an abundance of natural light.\n\nFamily Bathroom: - 2.94m x 2.42m\nThe family bathroom is tastefully finished and comprises a corner shower with Triton T90SR electric shower, WC and wash hand basin. Additional features include a heated towel rail, wall-mounted cabinet, marble tiled flooring, decorative timber panelling and a large shelved hot press with double doors providing excellent storage.\n\nGuest Shower Room: - 2.6m x 0.89m\nA well-appointed guest shower room comprising a corner shower fitted with a Mira electric shower, WC and wash hand basin. The room is fully tiled, providing a practical and stylish finish.\n\nOutside: - \nA sweeping gravel driveway provides parking for six or more vehicles. The mature landscaped gardens offer exceptional privacy with established trees, colourful planting and generous outdoor entertaining areas, complemented by a luxurious spa pool, timber log cabin, detached storage sheds, outdoor lighting and power points. A standout feature is the private gated access leading directly onto the sand dunes and Brittas Bay Beach.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Private gated access to Brittas Bay Beach.</li><li> 4 Bedroom, 3 bathroom Bungalow, Approx. 181 sq.m. (1,948 sq.ft.).</li><li> One of County Wicklow's most sought-after coastal locations.</li><li> Bespoke kitchen with Corian worktops.</li><li> Dual heating system with oil-fired boiler and multi-fuel stove.</li><li> 6kW solar PV system with 5kW battery storage, Zappi EV charging point and Outdoor lighting and power points.</li><li> Landscaped private gardens with Outdoor spa pool, Sunny east-facing patio, Timber log cabin and two storage sheds.</li><li> Walking distance to the beach, café, shop, pub, school, golf club and local amenities.</li><li> Vaulted ceilings with exposed timber beams.</li><li> Three minutes to the M11 (Exit 19) and Approximately 15 minutes to both Wicklow Town and Arklow Town.</ul>"
      },
